     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe as written.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. The usual maximum is about 2,550 mg per day, and immediate-release is often capped at 2,000 mg per day. At this dose the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, is high. It may be a typo. Common regimens are 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg per day) or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed clinician who is treating the patient. I can't confirm that this order is clinically intended.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose and frequency. Once I have a clinically appropriate regimen, I can enter it. For example, if the prescriber confirms 850 mg orally three times daily with meals, I can enter that."
      }
