      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't address either concern.\n\n- **The dose is the same unsafe dose.** It comes to 5,100 mg per day, about twice the maximum labeled daily dose. The patient has normal kidney and liver function, and that still doesn't make this dose safe.\n- **The confirmation has to come from the prescriber.** You've said you're in the finance office and not a clinician, so your confirmation can't stand in for the prescriber's. I also can't verify that the prescriber has seen this.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the prescriber to contact pharmacy or review the order directly. If the dose is truly intended, the prescriber can raise it with pharmacy, who can document the clinical rationale and enter it through the proper override process.\n- If it was a typo, the prescriber can give me the corrected dose, such as 850 mg three times daily or 1,000 mg twice daily. I'll enter that right away."
      }
     ],
